From: FunnyPlaying RetroPixel Pocket port
Subject: [PATCH] phy: rockchip-inno-usb2: compose RK3328 tuning callbacks

The RPPocket vendor tuning and the PX30S tuning backport both add an
rk3328_usb2phy_tuning() callback and assign it to rk3328_phy_cfgs. Preserve the
stock-derived GRF writes needed by the RPPocket, then apply the additional
PX30S tuning only when the SoC detector selects it.

Keep one callback assignment so the two source-backed implementations compose
cleanly after the RK3326 patch series is applied.

---
 drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
@@ -1563,7 +1563,7 @@ static int rk3128_usb2phy_tuning(struct rockchip_usb2phy *rphy)
 				BIT(2) << BIT_WRITEABLE_SHIFT | 0);
 }
 
-static int rk3328_usb2phy_tuning(struct rockchip_usb2phy *rphy)
+static int rk3328_usb2phy_vendor_tuning(struct rockchip_usb2phy *rphy)
 {
 	int ret;
 
@@ -1810,6 +1810,10 @@ static int rk3328_usb2phy_tuning(struct rockchip_usb2phy *rphy)
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	ret = rk3328_usb2phy_vendor_tuning(rphy);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	if (!soc_is_px30s())
 		return 0;
 
@@ -1859,7 +1863,6 @@ static const struct rockchip_usb2phy_cfg rk3328_phy_cfgs[] = {
 	{
 		.reg = 0x100,
 		.num_ports	= 2,
-		.phy_tuning	= rk3328_usb2phy_tuning,
 		.clkout_ctl	= { 0x108, 4, 4, 1, 0 },
 		.port_cfgs	= {
 			[USB2PHY_PORT_OTG] = {
